# GMS's readout ends "Final damage increases by 15% with each enemy pierced,
# and damage is doubled" -- one mechanic, not two: the arrow compounds x1.15
# per enemy, so the sixth takes 1.15^5 = 2.01x the first, which is the
# doubling. The swing draws the order it goes through them in, nothing here
# having a position. Worth +46% on a full six and nothing at all on one mob.
name: "Piercing Arrow"
skill_order: 1
description:
  "Fire an arrow through the enemies in front of you. Its damage grows with "
  "every enemy it has already pierced."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_CROSSBOWMAN
max_level: 20
base_delay_ms: 780
max_enemies: 6
lines: 4
pierce_gain_pct: 0.15
base { skill_pct: 0.92 }
per_level { skill_pct: 0.02 }
